{"surface": "event", "title": "Nvidia cuts its fiscal-2028 growth outlook on February 24", "html": "<div class=\"ev ws\"><div class=\"evh\"><h2 class=\"title\">Nvidia cuts its fiscal-2028 growth outlook on February 24</h2><p class=\"facts\"><span>The decision on Feb 24, 2027</span><span class=\"sep\">·</span><span class=\"src\">Known from Nvidia fiscal Q4 2027 earnings release and call</span></p><div class=\"hds\"><details class=\"hd\" data-k=\"definition\"><summary>Definition</summary><div class=\"hdb text\"><p>At its fiscal fourth-quarter report, projected for February 24, 2027, Nvidia lowers its outlook for fiscal-2028 revenue growth below the roughly 75% it gave on November 17, 2026, or withdraws it.</p></div></details><details class=\"hd\" data-k=\"notes\"><summary>Rationale</summary><div class=\"hdb\"><div class=\"note\" data-k=\"note:78\" data-note=\"note:78\"><div class=\"md\" data-md=\"Nvidia raised this outlook to 75% from 70% a week ago with demand ahead of supply, so a cut within one quarter needs something to change. Three things can: the 90-day licence deadline for overseas data centres serving Chinese customers falls about ten days before the report, on sales Luria puts at 5% to 20% of the total; customer financing (&#x27;access to capital for a large number of neoclouds is going to disappear&#x27; if Nvidia stops guaranteeing, per Apollo&#x27;s Rowan), with the $500 billion plan yet to fund a deal; and an interim or newly arrived CEO resetting the bar. One in five.\"><p>Nvidia raised this outlook to 75% from 70% a week ago with demand ahead of supply, so a cut within one quarter needs something to change. Three things can: the 90-day licence deadline for overseas data centres serving Chinese customers falls about ten days before the report, on sales Luria puts at 5% to 20% of the total; customer financing (&#x27;access to capital for a large number of neoclouds is going to disappear&#x27; if Nvidia stops guaranteeing, per Apollo&#x27;s Rowan), with the $500 billion plan yet to fund a deal; and an interim or newly arrived CEO resetting the bar. One in five.</p></div></div><div class=\"note\" data-k=\"note:85\" data-note=\"note:85\"><div class=\"md\" data-md=\"The downturn market&#x27;s triggers need Nvidia 50% below its record. A world where that has happened by May is one where demand, financing or export limits have visibly cut into orders, and about half of such worlds would show it as a lowered outlook at the February 24 report; the rest break later in the spring.\"><p>The downturn market&#x27;s triggers need Nvidia 50% below its record. A world where that has happened by May is one where demand, financing or export limits have visibly cut into orders, and about half of such worlds would show it as a lowered outlook at the February 24 report; the rest break later in the spring.</p></div></div><h4 class=\"ev-k\">Evidence</h4><div class=\"basis\"><p class=\"src\"><a class=\"go\" data-go=\"src:38\">benzinga.com</a></p><blockquote class=\"q\"><a class=\"go quote\" data-go=\"x:passage:src:38:43fdd08f7576\">After NVIDIA’s quarterly report, Luria said demand remained strong enough for the company to raise its fiscal 2028 growth outlook to 75% from 70%, even as it acknowledged uncertainty around Asian sales.</a></blockquote><blockquote class=\"q\"><a class=\"go quote\" data-go=\"x:passage:src:38:d5e8cdc1db9e\">Luria estimates that 5% to 20% of NVIDIA chip sales may have reached China directly or through resellers and Asian data centers, which drove his price-target reduction to $200 from $300, despite maintaining a Buy rating.</a></blockquote></div><div class=\"basis\"><p class=\"src\"><a class=\"go\" data-go=\"src:81\">benzinga.com</a></p><blockquote class=\"q\"><a class=\"go quote\" data-go=\"x:passage:src:81:50798bbcccdb\">Data centers that already serve those customers have 90 days to obtain a license. Operators are also expected to check who ultimately owns their clients, and a customer that refuses to answer is treated as a red flag.</a></blockquote></div><div class=\"basis\"><p class=\"src\"><a class=\"go\" data-go=\"src:18\">benzinga.com</a></p><blockquote class=\"q\"><a class=\"go quote\" data-go=\"x:passage:src:18:643b175e6a37\">On Tuesday’s Nvidia earnings call, Kress said the company would be selective about the deals it backs. Apollo CEO Marc Rowan told CNBC that if Nvidia stopped acting as guarantor, &quot;access to capital for a large number of neoclouds is going to disappear.&quot; Those companies buy chips and rent out the computing power.</a></blockquote></div></div></details></div></div><div class=\"strip\" data-count=\"5\" style=\"--cols:5\"><div class=\"sf first\" data-k=\"fig:Forecast\"><span class=\"lab\">Forecast</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:p:prop:29\"><span class=\"n v\">20.0%</span></a></span><a class=\"cap go calc\" data-go=\"x:p:prop:29\">How it’s set →</a></div><div class=\"sf\" data-k=\"fig:If Yes\"><span class=\"lab\">If Yes</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:outcome:prop:29:yes\"><span class=\"n v loss\">−$4,910</span></a></span><span class=\"cap\"><span class=\"n loss\">−0.98%</span> of portfolio</span></div><div class=\"sf\" data-k=\"fig:If No\"><span class=\"lab\">If No</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:outcome:prop:29:no\"><span class=\"n v gain\">+$1,227</span></a></span></div><div class=\"sf\" data-k=\"fig:Full impact\"><span class=\"lab\">Full impact</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:swing:prop:29\"><span class=\"n v loss\">−$6,137</span></a></span></div><div class=\"sf\" data-k=\"fig:Volatility\"><span class=\"lab\">Volatility</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:volatility:prop:29\"><span class=\"n v\">±$2,630</span></a></span></div></div><nav class=\"tabs\" role=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" data-tab=\"outcomes\">Outcomes</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" data-tab=\"probability\">Probability</but